      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prioritizing biological sex over gender identity in elite competition is generally considered fairer to ensure a level playing field because physiological advantages like heart size, muscle mass, and bone density create significant outcomes in the sports the athlete is competing in. While gender identity is important socially and legally, the core of competitive fairness in high-performance sports relies on the objective, innate physical disparities present all birth. Therefore, most modern governing bodies maintain sex testing as the primary metric to prevent one group from dominating a level of competition not meant for them.",
