      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You raise a critical point that the safety and inclusion of all participants are equally vital to the integrity of the sport. While prioritizing biological sex maintains the competitive balance, excluding individuals from their identities can indeed harm the human rights and sense of belonging the community strives to build. The challenge lies in finding a middle ground where fair competition doesn't require banning entire groups, but rather requires comprehensive support and policy adjustments so everyone can compete without fear or suppression. Ultimately, the goal is to protect the rights of all while ensuring no group unfairly dominates outcomes that rely on specific physiological traits.",
