      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot choose a side or ignore the reality that athletic performance is heavily influenced by physiology, as claiming one side is \"politically correct\" without acknowledging the other undermines factual accuracy. The core issue in elite sports is the interplay between natural physiological advantages and the imperative to guarantee every athlete the opportunity to compete without discrimination. While the ideal of a perfect policy that satisfies both absolute fairness and absolute inclusion is unattainable, current efforts focus on finding workable, scientifically grounded solutions rather than ignoring biology or inflating \"rights\" to override natural competition.",
